Drop tpm2_getekcertificate and the libcurl dependency

tpm2_getekcertificate fetches an EK certificate from the TPM vendor over
HTTP. It is the only tool that uses libcurl, but configure makes libcurl
mandatory and every tool is linked into the single tpm2 binary, so the
library ships with any image that carries tpm2-tools. On a device with no
network role that is an HTTP client nobody chose.

Remove the tool, its man page and the libcurl check. All other tools are
unchanged.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [TactiQ OS: no network client in the image]

--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -86,7 +86,6 @@
         AC_DEFINE([HAVE_FAPI_DIGEST_AND_SIGN], [1], [Support signing with restricted keys])],
         [])
 LIBS="${LIBS_save}"
-PKG_CHECK_MODULES([CURL], [libcurl])
 
 # pretty print of devicepath if efivar library is present
 # auto detect if not specified via the --with-efivar option.
--- a/Makefile.am
+++ b/Makefile.am
@@ -17,7 +17,7 @@
